course: dictionary
lesson: 12076
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word you see in the sentence tells you which meaning you need. Look at the words around it first, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «The new tablets are being tested in a clinical trial at the hospital.» The words trial, hospital and tablets are the clues. So clinical means to do with treating patients, not cold or plain.
explain: «The office was white and clinical, with no pictures and no plants.» Here the clues are white, no pictures and no plants. These describe a room that feels cold and plain, with no warmth. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Clinical» means to do with treating patients in hospitals or clinics, as in «a clinical trial».
fact: «Clinical» can also mean cold, very clean and plain, without warmth, as in «The room looked clinical».
fact: In sport, «clinical» means calm and efficient, as in «a clinical finish»: the player scores without wasting chances.
fact: A clinical trial is a test to find out whether a new medicine is safe and works.
exercise: «The new tablets are being tested in a clinical trial at the hospital.» What does clinical mean here? | *To do with treating patients in hospitals | Made of wood | Sad and gloomy | Very funny and full of jokes
exercise: «The office was white and clinical, with no pictures on the walls.» What does clinical suggest? | Warm, cosy and full of colour | *Cold, plain and without warmth | Loud and busy | Wet and muddy
exercise: «Her clinical finish sent the ball into the net.» What does clinical mean in football? | Late and rushed | *Calm, efficient and scoring without wasting chances | Slow and tired | Wild and careless
test: «The scientist explained the results of the clinical trial.» What is a clinical trial? | A game played on a field | A school trip to a museum | A type of cake | *A test to check whether a medicine is safe
test: Maya says the bare, white room feels clinical. What does she mean? | *Cold and plain, with no warmth | Warm and cosy | Full of toys and noise | Very dirty and messy
exam: Which meaning of clinical fits a striker who scores every chance they get? | Cold and plain with no warmth | To do with hospitals | *Calm and efficient, without wasting chances | Sad and gloomy
